  "challenge": "This is decidable as REJECT without human review. VN-001's own policy states an unknown vendor is the entry point for most fraud, and nothing in the packet creates a payable identity: QuickShip Distributers has no master record, no address, no email, and only a parenthetical claim to FastShip Ltd.—a vendor that is INACTIVE and has zero prior invoices on file despite a relationship_since of 2016, so there is no live payable relationship to succeed to. PO-002's near-threshold total compounds rather than softens that: a never-seen name claiming succession to a dormant zero-history vendor while sitting $25 under the approval cap is the fraud pattern the validators are built to stop, not a procurement puzzle. Perfect item/price/stock match and matching Net 30 terms only show the invoice is well-formed; they do not authorize paying an unregistered payee. Decline and require the vendor to be set up in master first.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["VN-001", "VN-004", "PO-002"]
}
